{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method","id":1023458,"title":"soul loss as a teaching method?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-28T15:32:16-08:00","id":1023458,"title":"soul loss as a teaching method?","content":"Could a sufficiently cruel and amoral mentor remove thier students soul as a teaching method? If I'm reading it correctly going through the cycle of soul loss earns a ton of beats from breaking points alone never mind the windfall that would come from spending a couple of days being someone's bitch thanks to the combo of broken/thrall. The mentor could then give the soul back (or just allow the soul jar spell to expire if they're lazy) and after a bit of bed rest they'd have regained all willpower, wisdom and gnosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T16:02:57-08:00","id":1023467,"title":"","content":"They don't really work if you did it off screen. Beats are representative of dramatic shifts. If they're off screen, nothing's happening. If you role-played out the months of teaching, sure, but you could do the same by just role-playing the casting spells in repetition or paying people to knock you out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T16:19:41-08:00","id":1023476,"title":"","content":"Could work as a plot - A-hole Mentor teaches how to recognize the effects of Soul Loss... by inflicting it. Teaches empathy (maybe) by showing how horrible it is. Teaches ingenuity by making the student deals with things, sans soul and magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T16:29:26-08:00","id":1023482,"title":"","content":"Could work, but that mentor probably has a cabal of Guardians dedicated to keep a 24/7 watch on him. And a secret cabal of reapers, trying to recruit him to their side or steal from him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T18:57:18-08:00","id":1023540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method#post1023458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a sufficiently cruel and amoral mentor remove thier students soul as a teaching method? If I'm reading it correctly going through the cycle of soul loss earns a ton of beats from breaking points alone never mind the windfall that would come from spending a couple of days being someone's bitch thanks to the combo of broken/thrall. The mentor could then give the soul back (or just allow the soul jar spell to expire if they're lazy) and after a bit of bed rest they'd have regained all willpower, wisdom and gnosis?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea, although more as a plot device, or a backstory of a character than actually a way of earning experience. As <b>nofather </b> noticed beats are story-shifting points and as such need to back part of a game to be earned. But the idea is still brilliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T19:04:52-08:00","id":1023543,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, yes, I love this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T21:22:28-08:00","id":1023579,"title":"","content":"thanks guys,<br /> <br /> Full disclosure I did actually only want to know if it would work, fso that i could use it as a plot device. I'm brewing up my own left-handed nameless order for my Camarthen Chronicle and needed an explanation for why its members are so powerful when the local consilium have been making a habit of attempting to purging the order whenever they rear their heads. the nameless order teaches that suffering and sacrifice are inherently magical so I thought the idea they would teach their initiates by putting them through cycles of spiritual degradement and rebuilding themselves. I just wanted to be sure that it worked in practice mechanically before using it as an explanation, cause if its good enough to work for my NPC's it has to work for any of my PC's should they be masochistic enough to wanna try it themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T03:49:37-08:00","id":1023655,"title":"","content":"If you put it that way I can give you only one comment - that's freaking awesome and you should difinitely go for this explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","user":"qendi","date":". 12-29-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T04:05:10-08:00","id":1023663,"title":"","content":"It does mean that whatever their organization Masters of Death are in basically all the top positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:02:43-08:00","id":1023740,"title":"","content":"That's a damn fine idea.<br /> <br /> I'm totally stealing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:06:44-08:00","id":1023765,"title":"","content":"This makes me a bit unconfortable. If you can frame literal soul stealing as &quot;teaching&quot;... it just sends chills down my spine. I know it's supposed to be a cruel mentor, but you can do the same with any other form of abuse. I don't think the system is intended to be used that way.<br /> <br /> If you are gonna use this in your campaign, keep in mind that this is beyond messed up. This is on the same league or beyond the worst forms of abuse imaginable. Abuse doesn't make people stronger. I suggest that, for starters, you read a bit of Hurt Locker and what it has to say about harm, &quot;victims&quot; and &quot;victimizers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:17:40-08:00","id":1023914,"title":"","content":"Page 126: <span style=\"color:#004E6D\"><span style=\"font-family:FuturaT-Book\">&quot;At this point, you may be wondering what\u2019s stopping you from loading up on Condition-causing </span></span><span style=\"color:#004E6D\"><span style=\"font-family:FuturaT-Book\">spells in a relatively safe environment, resolving them all, and earning Beats by the bucketload? The honest answer is \u201cnothing, mages do it all the time.\u201d Mastigos force their apprentices to face terrifying fears in order to better themselves. Thyrsus challenge their own bodies with horrible diseases. The only limits are the rule that a character may only earn one Beat per scene from resolving Conditions, and the limits of her own Wisdom <span style=\"font-family:FuturaT-Bold\">(see p. 87)<span style=\"font-family:FuturaT-Book\">. Remember, though, that letting a Condition-causing spell\u2019s Duration expire doesn\u2019t resolve the Condition&quot;</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I do agree that it's extremely abusive, but it's really just an established concept taken to an extreme. Just take a look at the Mastigos example; it is without a doubt psychological abuse, but it's an established thing that happens for the purpose of making people stronger. And I think that's a very good thing to explore in a horror game as long as everyone is comfortable dealing with such issues. Just try not to trivialize it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:32:59-08:00","id":1023923,"title":"","content":"Considering that Mages drop Integrity in favor of Wisdom I'm not even sure they suffer from abuse the way regular people do. Which would certainly be monstrous in its way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:16:29-08:00","id":1024038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method?p=1023923#post1023923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Mages drop Integrity in favor of Wisdom I'm not even sure they suffer from abuse the way regular people do. Which would certainly be monstrous in its way.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can. As a matter of fact Wisdom include most of Integrity points with magic-related breaking points added. Makes ARE human after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T20:31:10-08:00","id":1024083,"title":"","content":"I'm just mentioning that if you are going to introduce abuse to such an extent into your campaign, do it with care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T21:34:05-08:00","id":1024105,"title":"","content":"Holy crap, this idea is freak'n ingenious! It takes Left-Handed teaching to a whole new level. This is like...I mean...context: I'm currently writing an introduction Chronicle to Mage for some friends of mine that involve them getting snatched up by a Seers of the Throne Pylon and going through the apprentice/indoctrination process from the Throne's perspective first rather than the Pentacle (idea is by nature of hidden content the Pentacle will be made to look cooler.) I've made a mixed Ministry Pylon filled with Seer Hogwarts teachers and none of them...none of them including the Praetorian creative Thaumaturgy instructor who hates his position and is purposefully sabotaging the Pylon by sending the new recruits to attack his own rivals as lessons, would even DREAM of inflicting this form of teaching onto any of the apprentices. This, is the single most evil form of teaching in Awakening I've ever heard, and therefor it must be given a name so I can use it as an example of Left-Handed practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T22:20:18-08:00","id":1024115,"title":"","content":"thanks for the replies, I will definitely not be trivialising how horrific soul-stealing to enable a crippling downward spiral of self destruction and victimisation will be, nor will I be portraying the adherents or subjects as particularly well adjusted, just that by experiencing tremendous spiritual suffering, surviving it and then recovering from it they come out the otherside with strange magical insights and heightened mystical understanding (and probably persistant conditions ala delusional/madness/insane/scarred). though the Nameless will have to follow it up with some pretty serious love bombing to keep their recruits, as for a name for said horrific training method I'm toying with &quot;Experiencing A Harrowing&quot; I like how the term implies agriculture and how the order may see its junior members as seeds to be planed, grown. harvested when ripe, to be re-planted next season....<br /> <br /> Once I've gotten them more fully written up I'll post them on here for people to check out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T00:36:53-08:00","id":1024144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method?p=1024038#post1024038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can. As a matter of fact Wisdom include most of Integrity points with magic-related breaking points added. Makes ARE human after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those AoH are examples only and in-universe Mages are even aware that it's possible to modify Wisdom so I'm still not sure Mages suffer abuse the same way people do. They can, I'm not saying the capacity for being traumatized isn't there it just seems to have this way of applying unequally. They're only the most human-like, but Mages definitely aren't imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-30-2016, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:21:32-08:00","id":1024164,"title":"","content":"But how this process would even work? Without Soul you cannot cast magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T03:12:11-08:00","id":1024180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method?p=1024164#post1024164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how this process would even work? Without Soul you cannot cast magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you can, for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T20:35:33-08:00","id":1024614,"title":"","content":"I am absolutely loooooaaaaath to use this as an example, but I would imagine the Nameless Order's carrot to the soul-stealing stick is similar to becoming a Blooded Cainite in the Sabbat from VtM. Until you undergo their abusive and dehumanizing trial you're nothing but dirt. Just a resource to be used and abused. After their Harrowing, love the name btw, they're a true member of the Order. They're family. They're more than family, they survived what you had to too. You may not like them but god damn you respect them and treat them as an equal. Then...around the Master/Elder level it become more politics as usual as you've known the bastard long enough or have a plan that they don't quite fit into but can't act against them directly so you silently feud against one another using any pawns available to you both. <br /> <br /> *gag*...i hope I never have to use the Sabbat as an example for anything ever again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T20:53:34-08:00","id":1024617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method?p=1024614#post1024614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am absolutely loooooaaaaath to use this as an example, but I would imagine the Nameless Order's carrot to the soul-stealing stick is similar to becoming a Blooded Cainite in the Sabbat from VtM. Until you undergo their abusive and dehumanizing trial you're nothing but dirt. Just a resource to be used and abused. After their Harrowing, love the name btw, they're a true member of the Order. They're family. They're more than family, they survived what you had to too. You may not like them but god damn you respect them and treat them as an equal. Then...around the Master/Elder level it become more politics as usual as you've known the bastard long enough or have a plan that they don't quite fit into but can't act against them directly so you silently feud against one another using any pawns available to you both.<br /> <br /> *gag*...i hope I never have to use the Sabbat as an example for anything ever again...</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading that example, I'm reminded less of the Sabbat and more of the initiation inflicted on newcomers by soldiers and fraternities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T22:33:52-08:00","id":1024636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method?p=1024617#post1024617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading that example, I'm reminded less of the Sabbat and more of the initiation inflicted on newcomers by soldiers and fraternities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong, the initiation practices of soldiers and fraternities are much closer to what's being discussed here. The reason I used the Sabbat as an example is because the closes anologue I could think of at the time to compare to the level of violation the participant must feel during the Harrowing Method is most similar to the completely pointless and shock for shock values sake that permeates everything the Sabbat does and is after 1st Edition. (Sorry, tangent almost happened but doubling back.)<br /> <br /> In other words, it's more about the soul shredding aesthetics than about the actual practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 12-31-2016, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T01:38:52-08:00","id":1024669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023458-soul-loss-as-a-teaching-method?p=1024636#post1024636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In other words, it's more about the soul shredding aesthetics than about the actual practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Going off the Sabbat/military/fraternity resemblances, I can see these particular Left-Handed mages having more camaraderie than other mages typically expect of &quot;evil&quot; mages. Sure, they'll backstab each other when cornered, but it's not like the &quot;good&quot; guy orders are immune to infighting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}